---
layout: base.njk
title: Rules
pageId: rules
---
{% block content %}
<header class="page-heading">
  <p class="eyebrow">How to play</p>
  <h1>Rules of the water</h1>
  <p>Find hidden ships by choosing untouched squares. Daily Waters is a solo score challenge; Two Players is a turn-based match.</p>
</header>

<section class="rules-overview" aria-labelledby="shared-rules-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Both game types</p>
  <h2 id="shared-rules-title" class="visually-hidden">Rules shared by Daily Waters and Two Players</h2>
  <div class="rules-grid">
    <section class="rule-block">
      <span class="rule-number">01</span>
      <h3>Fire</h3>
      <p>Choose one untouched square. Every square can be fired on only once.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="rule-block">
      <span class="rule-number">02</span>
      <h3>Read</h3>
      <p>A miss becomes unavailable grey water, a hit turns red, and a fully sunk ship changes to the sunk colour.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="rule-block">
      <span class="rule-number">03</span>
      <h3>Sink</h3>
      <p>Complete the game by finding every occupied square. The hit queue and fleet list show your progress.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="rules-section" aria-labelledby="game-types-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Choose your game</p>
  <h2 id="game-types-title">Two different challenges</h2>
  <div class="rules-details rules-details--modes">
    <article>
      <span class="rule-number">01 · Solo</span>
      <h3>Daily Waters</h3>
      <p>No placement and no turns. Everyone receives the same standard fleet for the UTC day. Sink all five ships, then share your result and compare scores—the player who finishes in the fewest total shots wins. Progress is saved in this browser for the day.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span class="rule-number">02 · Two players</span>
      <h3>Private match</h3>
      <p>Each player places a private fleet, then takes one shot per turn. The first player to sink the opposing fleet wins; resigning awards the win to the opponent.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="rules-section" aria-labelledby="placement-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Two-player setup</p>
  <h2 id="placement-title">Place your ships</h2>
  <p class="rules-section__lede">Both players arrange and lock their own fleet before the first turn. Ships may be horizontal or vertical, but cannot overlap, touch—even diagonally—or leave the board. Your opponent cannot see your positions.</p>
  <ol class="placement-steps">
    <li>
      <span>01</span>
      <div><strong>Drag to place</strong><p>Drag a ship from the fleet list onto any valid board square. Drag a placed ship again to move it.</p></div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span>02</span>
      <div><strong>Tap to rotate</strong><p>Tap or click a placed ship once to rotate it. You can also select a ship and use the Rotate button.</p></div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span>03</span>
      <div><strong>Return to the fleet</strong><p>Double-tap or double-click a placed ship, or drag it back onto the fleet list. Random and Clear remain available.</p></div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span>04</span>
      <div><strong>Lock when ready</strong><p>Lock your fleet after every ship is placed. Positions cannot be changed after locking, and play starts only when both fleets are locked.</p></div>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p class="rules-note"><strong>Keyboard:</strong> focus a fleet ship and press Enter to move to the first valid starting square on the board. Until you place it, the arrow keys move focus and the other ships stay locked. Press Enter to place it. Once placed, an arrow key moves the ship to the next valid position in that direction, skipping blocked areas. Press Enter to rotate it or Delete to return it to the fleet.</p>
</section>

<section class="rules-section" aria-labelledby="match-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Two-player match</p>
  <h2 id="match-title">Take turns</h2>
  <div class="rules-details">
    <article>
      <h3>Read the board</h3>
      <p>Misses become unavailable grey squares, hits turn red, and a fully sunk ship changes to the sunk colour. The turn banner and browser-tab title tell you when to play.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Follow your progress</h3>
      <p>The hit queue shows how many fleet squares you have found. The fleet list marks each fully sunk opposing ship in red without revealing unfinished ship positions.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Finish the match</h3>
      <p>You may resign at any time, immediately giving the win to your opponent. When a match ends, both final fleets and the complete boards remain visible.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="fleet-table" aria-labelledby="fleets-title">
  <h2 id="fleets-title">Game formats</h2>
  <div><strong>Daily</strong><span>10 × 10 board</span><span>5, 4, 3, 3, 2</span></div>
  <div><strong>Quick match</strong><span>7 × 7 board</span><span>3, 2, 2</span></div>
  <div><strong>Standard match</strong><span>10 × 10 board</span><span>5, 4, 3, 3, 2</span></div>
</section>
{% endblock %}
